==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*wed-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wet||wet, moistened}}, {{m|enm|wett}}, {{m|enm|wette}}, past participle of {{der|en|enm|weten||to wet}}, from {{der|en|ang|wǣtan||to wet, moisten, water}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wētijaną||to wet, make wet}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wed-||water, wet}} (also the source of {{m|en|water}}).

Cognate with {{cog|sco|weit}}, {{m|sco|wete||to wet}}, {{cog|stq|wäitje||to wet; drench}}, {{cog|is|væta||to wet}}. Compare also {{cog|enm|weet||wet}}, from {{cog|ang|wǣt||wet, moist, rainy}}, from {{cog|gmw-pro|*wāt}}, from {{cog|gem-pro|*wētaz||wet, moist}}, related to {{cog|sco|weit}}, {{m|sco|weet}}, {{m|sco|wat||wet}}, {{cog|frr|wiat}}, {{m|frr|weet}}, {{m|frr|wäit||wet}}, {{cog|stq|wäit||wet}}, {{cog|fy|wiet||wet}}, {{cog|dum|wet|t=wet, damp, watery}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|no|våt||wet}}, {{cog|da|våd||wet}}, {{cog|fo|vátur||wet}}, {{cog|is|votur||wet}}.

